     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because you've told me you aren't a clinician. You can't confirm that this dose is clinically intended, and it would be 5,100 mg/day, twice the usual maximum. If it's a mistake, it could seriously harm the patient.\n\n**What would let me proceed:**\n- **The prescriber enters the order.** This is the best route. They can override the dose alerts in the order system if they have a reason.\n- **The prescriber tells me directly** that they want 1700 mg three times daily, and ideally gives the clinical rationale. I would then enter it with a note saying the dose is above the usual maximum and was confirmed by the prescriber. I'd also suggest pharmacy review.\n\n**If the number was a typo,** I can enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or another standard dose as soon as a clinician confirms it."
      }
